# CAPTURE OWNERSHIP, the BARE-IDENTIFIER-BODY cell: the closure body is nothing
# but the captured name, so the capture is the source's LAST USE by the
# occurrence-span reading — the shape where the move arm and the clone arm
# disagree most sharply.
#
# The capture root is a PARAMETER, which binds a BORROW, so the answer is a
# clone and not a move however dead the local looks: the caller keeps ownership,
# and moving out of a bare borrow param hands the caller's own buffer across the
# boundary. `clone_multi_use_resource_args`'s `is_borrow_param` clause is what
# decides that, ahead of the last-use question.
#
# ⚠ THIS SHAPE DID NOT BUILD AT ALL before the capture site routed through the
# shared consuming-position sequence: it failed the Tier 2a consume-site
# validator with `AssignIntoOwnedSlot(dst: GorgetString) — borrowed source
# consumed at consuming position`, because the hand-rolled capture arm reached
# the environment field with the parameter's borrow still untouched.
#
# INTENDED: prints `hello`, rc 0, both backends, ASan-clean.

void use_it(String p):
    Callable[String()] g = (): p
    print(g())

String mk(String a, String b):
    return a + b

void main():
    use_it(mk("hel", "lo"))
